<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  Bullet airframe - URDF for Gazebo (Harmonic) / ROS 2
  REV 2026-10-14e: base_link CG moved 20 mm forward, x = 0.3071 -> 0.2871
  (design change, e.g. battery relocated forward). With the spec CG the wing
  c/4 sat 35 mm ahead of the vehicle CG and the airframe was statically
  unstable in pitch (porpoising in PX4 SITL); 20 mm forward puts the CG ahead
  of the neutral point. Inertia about the CG kept from the spec sheet
  (relocated mass, not added ballast). Spec-sheet value kept in comments.
  REV 2026-10-14d: airframe geometry rolled +90 deg about the fuselage axis
  (tools/roll_urdf.py). The CAD meshes put the main wing (straight, tapered,
  symmetric airfoil, 400 mm span, x = 0.19..0.27) along the old +Z axis, so with
  +Z up the wing stood vertical. Visual/collision origins, rotor joint origins
  and the base_link inertia (Iyy <-> Izz) were rotated; the wing now spans Y
  and lies in the X-Y plane. Mass, CG, rotor and Gazebo parameters unchanged.
  REV 2026-10-14c: mass properties and aerodynamics updated from the CFD
  engineer's spec sheet (3.3626 kg configuration). Geometry, meshes, rotors
  and collisions carried over unchanged from rev 2026-10-13b.

  ===================== FRAME CONVENTION =====================
    origin  = nose apex, on the fuselage axis
    +X      = AFT  along the fuselage   (nose x=0, tail disc x=0.600)
    +Y      = starboard
    +Z      = up
  Forward flight is -X. A body_flu frame (x forward, y port, z up) is
  provided below for plugins that assume the PX4/Gazebo FLU convention.

  ===================== CFD SPEC SHEET -> URDF MAPPING =====================
  CFD frame: X tail-to-nose (forward), Y up, Z starboard, origin nose apex.
      X_urdf = -X_cfd      Y_urdf = Z_cfd      Z_urdf = Y_cfd
  Spec-sheet positions are "from nose", read as distances measured aft and
  therefore entered as +x here. CONFIRMED PENDING: engineer to verify +Z_cfd
  is the starboard side (see reconciliation note).

  Inertia remap (axis relabelling):
      Ixx_urdf = Ixx_cfd    Iyy_urdf = Izz_cfd    Izz_urdf = Iyy_cfd
  REV d: the meshes show the wing spanning the old Z_urdf (= Y_cfd per the
  mapping above), i.e. the mesh 'up' axis is not Y_cfd. After the roll the
  inertia entries are Iyy = 0.1037, Izz = 0.1031 (0.6 % apart). ENGINEER TO
  CONFIRM the CFD axis mapping against the CAD export.

  ===================== ASSUMPTIONS MADE IN THIS REVISION =================
  A1. The spec-sheet inertias (Iyy 0.4208, Izz 0.4202) are ABOUT THE NOSE
      ORIGIN, not the CG. 0.4208 - m*xcg^2 = 0.4208 - 3.3626*0.3071^2 = 0.1037,
      which is physically consistent with a 0.6 m, 3.4 kg body. The values
      entered below are the CG-corrected ones. Engineer to confirm or supply
      CG-referenced tensors.
  A2. No products of inertia on the spec sheet; set to zero. The previous
      revision had ixz = 4.9e-4; request a full tensor.
  A3. The spec-sheet mass (3.3626 kg) is assumed to EXCLUDE the four
      propellers, which remain separate rotor links at 21 g each. If it
      includes them, subtract 0.084 kg from base_link.
  A4. Ycg = Zcg = 0 taken literally (previous rev had -0.027 mm / -2.3 mm).
  A5. The wing (0.1094 m^2, c/4 at x = 0.2776) is NOT present as a separate
      visual/collision in this URDF; it is either inside airframe.stl or
      absent from the CAD export. It IS modelled aerodynamically below.
  A6. Gazebo's LiftDrag system has no constant-drag (CD0) term; cda is a
      drag slope in alpha. CD0 for the body (0.00703 on frontal area) and the
      wing (0.0528 on wing area) must be applied by a custom plugin or by the
      vehicle dynamics package. Placeholder noted in the plugin blocks.
-->
<robot name="bullet">

  <material name="carbon">
    <color rgba="0.13 0.13 0.15 1.0"/>
  </material>
  <material name="motor_grey">
    <color rgba="0.45 0.45 0.48 1.0"/>
  </material>
  <material name="rotor_dark">
    <color rgba="0.08 0.08 0.09 1.0"/>
  </material>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- base_link : airframe + motors + wing + all fixed internal mass     -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <link name="base_link">

    <inertial>
      <!-- Spec sheet: Xcg 0.3071 m from nose, Ycg 0, Zcg 0.
           REV e: moved 20 mm forward to 0.2871 for static pitch stability. -->
      <origin xyz="0.2871 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <!-- Spec sheet: 3.3626 kg (see assumption A3) -->
      <mass value="3.3626"/>
      <!-- About the CG, kg*m^2, after remap and nose->CG correction (A1, A2):
             Ixx = 0.0496 (roll about fuselage axis, same axis in both frames)
             Iyy = Izz_cfd - m*xcg^2 = 0.4202 - 0.3171 = 0.1031 (pitch, about starboard)
             Izz = Iyy_cfd - m*xcg^2 = 0.4208 - 0.3171 = 0.1037 (yaw, about up) -->
      <inertia ixx="4.960000000e-02" ixy="0.000000000e+00" ixz="0.000000000e+00"
                                     iyy="1.037000000e-01" iyz="0.000000000e+00"
                                                           izz="1.031000000e-01"/>
    </inertial>

    <visual name="airframe_visual">
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/airframe.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="carbon"/>
    </visual>

    <!-- Motor hub end at x = 0.500 (spec sheet) - matches CAD occurrence -->
    <visual name="motor_0_visual">
      <origin xyz="0.499999999 -0.137732833 0.137732833" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/motor_0.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="motor_grey"/>
    </visual>
    <visual name="motor_1_visual">
      <origin xyz="0.499999999 -0.137732833 -0.137732833" rpy="-1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/motor_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="motor_grey"/>
    </visual>
    <visual name="motor_2_visual">
      <origin xyz="0.499999999 0.137732833 0.137732833" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/motor_2.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="motor_grey"/>
    </visual>
    <visual name="motor_3_visual">
      <origin xyz="0.499999999 0.137732833 -0.137732833" rpy="-1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/motor_3.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="motor_grey"/>
    </visual>

    <!-- COLLISION: primitive approximation, unchanged from rev 2026-10-13b. -->
    <collision name="col_nose">
      <origin xyz="0.03 0 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.060 0.060 0.060"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_forebody">
      <origin xyz="0.1175 0 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.115 0.116 0.116"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_midbody">
      <origin xyz="0.3125 0 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.275 0.125 0.125"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_boattail">
      <origin xyz="0.525 0 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.150 0.108 0.108"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_fin_upper">
      <origin xyz="0.22765 -0.13125 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.0803 0.0126 0.1375"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_fin_lower">
      <origin xyz="0.22765 0.13125 0" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
      <geometry><box size="0.0803 0.0126 0.1375"/></geometry>
    </collision>

    <collision name="col_boom_0">
      <origin xyz="0.5545 -0.221 0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.0046" length="0.200"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_boom_1">
      <origin xyz="0.5545 -0.221 -0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.0046" length="0.200"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_boom_2">
      <origin xyz="0.5545 0.221 0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.0046" length="0.200"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_boom_3">
      <origin xyz="0.5545 0.221 -0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.0046" length="0.200"/></geometry>
    </collision>

    <collision name="col_stub_0">
      <origin xyz="0.68 -0.221 0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.007" length="0.010"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_stub_1">
      <origin xyz="0.68 -0.221 -0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.007" length="0.010"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_stub_2">
      <origin xyz="0.68 0.221 0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.007" length="0.010"/></geometry>
    </collision>
    <collision name="col_stub_3">
      <origin xyz="0.68 0.221 -0.221" rpy="1.57079633 0 1.57079633"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.007" length="0.010"/></geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- body_flu : x forward, y port, z up, at the CG. For PX4/Gazebo      -->
  <!-- plugins that assume FLU. Fixed joint; lumped into base_link by     -->
  <!-- the SDF converter and exposed as a frame.                          -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <link name="body_flu"/>
  <joint name="body_flu_joint" type="fixed">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="body_flu"/>
    <origin xyz="0.2871 0 0" rpy="0 0 3.141592654"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- rotor_0 : -y +z quadrant, blade handedness A                      -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <link name="rotor_0">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.021000000"/>
      <inertia ixx="4.746789149e-05" ixy="-1.732341579e-12" ixz="-1.007788708e-11"
                                     iyy="4.768615918e-05"  iyz="3.651673200e-09"
                                                            izz="9.169536207e-07"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual name="rotor_0_visual">
      <origin xyz="-0.006350301 0.000001991 -0.000009377" rpy="0 0 -1.570796327"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/propeller_0.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="rotor_dark"/>
    </visual>
    <collision name="rotor_0_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.003619 0 0" rpy="0 1.570796327 0"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.113750" length="0.030318"/></geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <joint name="rotor_0_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="rotor_0"/>
    <origin xyz="0.548222132 -0.137732767 0.137732823" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
    <dynamics damping="0.0" friction="0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- rotor_1 : -y -z quadrant, blade handedness B                      -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <link name="rotor_1">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.021000000"/>
      <inertia ixx="4.746789149e-05" ixy="1.732341579e-12"  ixz="-1.007788738e-11"
                                     iyy="4.768615918e-05"  iyz="-3.651673200e-09"
                                                            izz="9.169536207e-07"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual name="rotor_1_visual">
      <origin xyz="-0.006350301 -0.000001991 -0.000009377" rpy="3.141592654 0 1.570796327"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/propeller_1.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="rotor_dark"/>
    </visual>
    <collision name="rotor_1_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.003619 0 0" rpy="0 1.570796327 0"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.113750" length="0.030318"/></geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <joint name="rotor_1_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="rotor_1"/>
    <origin xyz="0.548222132 -0.137732767 -0.137732823" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
    <dynamics damping="0.0" friction="0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- rotor_2 : +y +z quadrant, blade handedness B                      -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <link name="rotor_2">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.021000000"/>
      <inertia ixx="4.746789149e-05" ixy="-1.732341579e-12" ixz="1.007788738e-11"
                                     iyy="4.768615918e-05"  iyz="-3.651673200e-09"
                                                            izz="9.169536207e-07"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual name="rotor_2_visual">
      <origin xyz="-0.006350301 0.000001991 0.000009377" rpy="0 0 -1.570796327"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/propeller_2.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="rotor_dark"/>
    </visual>
    <collision name="rotor_2_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.003619 0 0" rpy="0 1.570796327 0"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.113750" length="0.030318"/></geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <joint name="rotor_2_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="rotor_2"/>
    <origin xyz="0.548222132 0.137732767 0.137732823" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
    <dynamics damping="0.0" friction="0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- rotor_3 : +y -z quadrant, blade handedness A                      -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <link name="rotor_3">
    <inertial>
      <origin xyz="0 0 0" rpy="0 0 0"/>
      <mass value="0.021000000"/>
      <inertia ixx="4.746789149e-05" ixy="1.732341579e-12"  ixz="1.007788708e-11"
                                     iyy="4.768615918e-05"  iyz="3.651673200e-09"
                                                            izz="9.169536207e-07"/>
    </inertial>
    <visual name="rotor_3_visual">
      <origin xyz="-0.006350301 -0.000001991 0.000009377" rpy="3.141592654 0 1.570796327"/>
      <geometry>
        <mesh filename="package://bullet_sim/meshes/visual/propeller_3.stl" scale="0.001 0.001 0.001"/>
      </geometry>
      <material name="rotor_dark"/>
    </visual>
    <collision name="rotor_3_collision">
      <origin xyz="0.003619 0 0" rpy="0 1.570796327 0"/>
      <geometry><cylinder radius="0.113750" length="0.030318"/></geometry>
    </collision>
  </link>
  <joint name="rotor_3_joint" type="continuous">
    <parent link="base_link"/>
    <child link="rotor_3"/>
    <origin xyz="0.548222132 0.137732767 -0.137732823" rpy="1.57079633 0 0"/>
    <axis xyz="1 0 0"/>
    <dynamics damping="0.0" friction="0.0"/>
  </joint>

  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <!-- AERODYNAMICS (Gazebo Harmonic LiftDrag systems)                    -->
  <!-- Positions are in the base_link frame (origin nose apex).           -->
  <!-- forward = -X (flight direction), upward = +Z.                      -->
  <!-- Coefficients are per radian. alpha positive nose-up.               -->
  <!-- ================================================================= -->
  <gazebo>

    <!-- WING. Spec sheet: area 0.1094009 m^2, c/4 at 0.2776 m from nose,
         CLalpha 3.621 /rad, Cmalpha -0.6 /rad (wrt wing area), CD0 0.052792.
         TODO (A6): CD0 not representable here; cda below is the drag SLOPE
         and is a placeholder until the engineer supplies dCD/dalpha and the
         aspect ratio for induced drag. Stall values are placeholders.
         VERIFY: whether this LiftDrag build multiplies cma by a reference
         chord; if not, scale cma by the mean aerodynamic chord. -->
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-lift-drag-system" name="gz::sim::systems::LiftDrag">
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <air_density>1.225</air_density>
      <area>0.1094009</area>
      <a0>0.0</a0>
      <cla>3.621</cla>
      <cda>0.05</cda>            <!-- PLACEHOLDER: dCD/dalpha, not CD0 -->
      <cma>-0.6</cma>
      <alpha_stall>0.26</alpha_stall>  <!-- 15 deg placeholder -->
      <cla_stall>-2.0</cla_stall>      <!-- placeholder -->
      <cda_stall>1.0</cda_stall>       <!-- placeholder -->
      <cma_stall>0.0</cma_stall>
      <cp>0.2776 0 0</cp>
      <forward>-1 0 0</forward>
      <upward>0 0 1</upward>
    </plugin>

    <!-- FUSELAGE normal force. Spec sheet gives the body CP at 0.392 m
         (alpha 0 deg) and 0.329 m (alpha 2 deg) and CD0 0.0070325 on a
         frontal area of 0.0145734 m^2, but no body normal-force slope.
         Slender-body estimate CNalpha ~ 2.0 /rad on frontal area entered as
         a placeholder; cp set to the alpha = 0 value. Engineer to supply
         CNalpha and a CP-vs-alpha table (the 63 mm shift over 2 deg should be
         checked at 4 deg). -->
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-lift-drag-system" name="gz::sim::systems::LiftDrag">
      <link_name>base_link</link_name>
      <air_density>1.225</air_density>
      <area>0.0145734</area>
      <a0>0.0</a0>
      <cla>2.0</cla>             <!-- PLACEHOLDER slender-body CNalpha -->
      <cda>0.02</cda>            <!-- PLACEHOLDER slope; CD0 0.00703 handled separately (A6) -->
      <cma>0.0</cma>
      <alpha_stall>0.5</alpha_stall>
      <cla_stall>0.0</cla_stall>
      <cda_stall>0.0</cda_stall>
      <cma_stall>0.0</cma_stall>
      <cp>0.392 0 0</cp>
      <forward>-1 0 0</forward>
      <upward>0 0 1</upward>
    </plugin>

    <!-- Lateral (sideslip) equivalents of both surfaces are omitted until
         beta-derivatives are available; add duplicate blocks with
         upward = 0 1 0 when they are. -->

  </gazebo>

</robot>
